>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `set_subgoaler`

``` hol4
simpLib.set_subgoaler : Traverse.subgoaler -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sets the procedure that reduces side conditions before the solvers.

A subgoaler has type `Traverse.simp_prover_ctxt -> term -> thm` (see
[`simpLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpLib.add_unsafe_solver)) and returns
`|- c = c'` for a side condition `c`. If `c'` is `T`, `c` is proved;
otherwise the unsafe solvers are tried on `c'`. The default subgoaler
simplifies `c` recursively. `set_subgoaler subgoaler ss` replaces the
subgoaler of `ss`; the default cannot be restored.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> fun arith_subgoaler _ c = EQT_INTRO (DECIDE c);
>> SIMP_CONV (simpLib.set_subgoaler arith_subgoaler bool_ss)
     [arithmeticTheory.LESS_MOD] “x MOD (x + 1)”;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpLib.add_unsafe_solver),
[`simpLib.set_cond_depth`](#simpLib.set_cond_depth).
